    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Spoon and Rafter is the fourth album by Mojave 3, released in 2003 on 4AD. It finds the band refining its trademark blend of country-rock, folk, and dream-pop into a warmer, more expansive sound, with reviews noting a shift toward more collaborative arrangements and a more richly textured palette.\n\nThe album opens with the long, drifting “Bluebird of Happiness” and moves through hazy, melodic songs such as “Starlite #1,” “Billoddity,” and “Writing to St. Peter,” balancing melancholy with a gentle, luminous tone. Critics generally responded positively, with the record earning a 76 on Metacritic, and it later gained wider recognition through the use of “Billoddity” and “Bluebird of Happiness” in The O.C.",
